hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16755","He said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah, he said: Nafi narrated to me, from Safiyya, from some of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever comes to a fortune-teller and believes him in what he says, his prayer is not accepted for forty days."
"23610","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us from Ubaydullah, Nafi' narrated to me from Safiyyah from one of the wives of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever comes to a fortune-teller and believes him in what he says, his prayer will not be accepted for forty days."
"23611","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi and Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us from Malik from Sumayy from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman from one of the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was seen at al-Arj pouring water over his head while fasting, from heat or thirst."
